#X msg 110 619 @mode;
#X text 245 619 Get/Set output mode. 'full' - output the cross-correlation
at each point of overlap \, with an output length of (M+N-1). At the
end-points of the cross-correlation \, the signals do not overlap completely
\, and boundary effects may be seen. 'valid' - output of length (max(M
\, N)-min(M \, N)+1). The cross-correlation product is only given for
points where the signals overlap completely. Values outside the signal
boundary have no effect. 'same' - output of length max(M \, N). Boundary
effects are still visible. Type: symbol. Default value: valid. Allowed
values: valid \, same \, full.;
